Input: {"question": "Which award did Galopim de Carvalho receive?", "source_segments": {"D1S1": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 0, "end": 95, "text": "**Portuguese Professor and Author Galopim de Carvalho Honored with Prestigious Prémio Bordalo**"}, "D1S2": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 97, "end": 285, "text": "Lisbon, Portugal - Renowned Portuguese professor and author, Galopim de Carvalho, has been awarded the esteemed Prémio Bordalo, a prestigious prize created by the Casa da Imprensa in 1962."}, "D1S3": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 286, "end": 431, "text": "This recognition is a testament to Carvalho's outstanding contributions to the literary world and his dedication to promoting Portuguese culture."}, "D1S4": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 432, "end": 602, "text": "The Prémio Bordalo, initially known as the Óscar da Imprensa, is one of the most respected awards in Portugal, recognizing excellence in journalism, literature, and arts."}, "D1S5": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 603, "end": 820, "text": "Since its inception, the prize has been bestowed upon some of the most distinguished figures in Portuguese culture, and Galopim de Carvalho's receipt of this honor is a significant milestone in his illustrious career."}, "D1S6": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 821, "end": 1002, "text": "\"Galopim de Carvalho is a towering figure in Portuguese literature, and this award is a well-deserved recognition of his tireless efforts to promote our cultural heritage,\" said Dr."}, "D1S7": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1003, "end": 1093, "text": "Maria João Marques, a prominent literary critic and professor at the University of Lisbon."}, "D1S8": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1094, "end": 1248, "text": "\"His work has inspired generations of writers, scholars, and readers alike, and we are proud to count him among our nation's most esteemed intellectuals.\""}, "D1S9": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1249, "end": 1349, "text": "Carvalho's extensive body of work spans multiple genres, including fiction, non-fiction, and poetry."}, "D1S10": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1350, "end": 1510, "text": "His writing is characterized by its lyricism, depth, and insight into the human condition, earning him widespread acclaim both domestically and internationally."}, "D1S11": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1511, "end": 1722, "text": "According to data from the Portuguese National Library, Carvalho's books have been translated into numerous languages, including English, French, Spanish, and German, demonstrating the global appeal of his work."}, "D1S12": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1723, "end": 1908, "text": "Furthermore, his literary contributions have been recognized by various institutions, including the Portuguese Ministry of Culture, which has awarded him several grants and fellowships."}, "D1S13": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1909, "end": 2143, "text": "\"Galopim de Carvalho's receipt of the Prémio Bordalo is a testament to the power of literature to bring people together and foster greater understanding between cultures,\" said António Mega Ferreira, President of the Casa da Imprensa."}, "D1S14": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2144, "end": 2245, "text": "\"We are honored to recognize his achievements and celebrate his contributions to Portuguese culture.\""}, "D1S15": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2246, "end": 2480, "text": "In a statement, Galopim de Carvalho expressed his gratitude for the award, saying, \"I am deeply humbled by this recognition, and I accept it not only as a personal honor but also as a tribute to the rich cultural heritage of Portugal."}, "D2S1": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 0, "end": 19, "text": "Galopim de Carvalho"}, "D2S2": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 21, "end": 202, "text": "Galopim de Carvalho is a Portuguese professor and author, best known for her brief foray into acting, which culminated in her receiving the Golden Raspberry Award for Worst Actress."}, "D2S3": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 203, "end": 224, "text": "Early Life and Career"}, "D2S4": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 226, "end": 297, "text": "Galopim de Carvalho was born on February 12, 1955, in Lisbon, Portugal."}, "D2S5": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 298, "end": 347, "text": "She pursued a career in academia, earning a Ph.D."}, "D2S6": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 348, "end": 400, "text": "in Literature from the University of Lisbon in 1985."}, "D2S7": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 401, "end": 532, "text": "She went on to become a respected professor of Portuguese literature, publishing several critically acclaimed books on the subject."}, "D2S8": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 533, "end": 552, "text": "Venture into Acting"}, "D2S9": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 554, "end": 651, "text": "In the early 2000s, Galopim de Carvalho decided to explore her creative side by taking up acting."}, "D2S10": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 652, "end": 774, "text": "She made her film debut in the 2003 Portuguese drama \"O Rio do Tempo\" (The River of Time), playing the lead role of Maria."}, "D2S11": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 775, "end": 859, "text": "Despite her lack of experience, she was praised by critics for her bold performance."}, "D2S12": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 860, "end": 1034, "text": "However, her subsequent roles in the 2005 films \"A Noite dos Vampiros\" (The Night of the Vampires) and \"O Amor É um Jogo\" (Love is a Game) were met with widespread criticism."}, "D2S13": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1035, "end": 1131, "text": "Her performances were panned by critics, with many considering them to be amateurish and wooden."}, "D2S14": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1132, "end": 1172, "text": "Golden Raspberry Award for Worst Actress"}, "D2S15": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1174, "end": 1327, "text": "In 2006, Galopim de Carvalho received the Golden Raspberry Award for Worst Actress for her performances in \"A Noite dos Vampiros\" and \"O Amor É um Jogo\"."}, "D2S16": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1328, "end": 1468, "text": "This award, also known as the Razzie, is an annual accolade that recognizes the worst films, actors, directors, and screenplays of the year."}, "D2S17": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1469, "end": 1491, "text": "Studies and References"}, "D2S18": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1493, "end": 1688, "text": "A study published in the Journal of Film Studies in 2007 analyzed Galopim de Carvalho's acting style and concluded that her lack of experience and training led to her poor performances on screen."}, "D2S19": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1689, "end": 1692, "text": "[1]"}, "D2S20": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1694, "end": 1924, "text": "In an interview with the Portuguese newspaper Público in 2008, Galopim de Carvalho acknowledged her mistakes and stated that she had returned to her academic pursuits, citing a greater sense of fulfillment in teaching and writing."}, "D2S21": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1925, "end": 1928, "text": "[2]"}, "D2S22": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1930, "end": 2189, "text": "A book titled \"The Razzie Awards: A History of Hollywood's Biggest Fails\" by film critic John Wilson, published in 2010, features a chapter dedicated to Galopim de Carvalho's Golden Raspberry Award win, providing a detailed account of her brief acting career."}}, "candidates": [], "original_cards": [], "initial_answers": ["Prémio Bordalo", "Golden Raspberry Award for Worst Actress"]}
